\name{ProjectBundle}
\alias{ProjectBundle}
\title{Create, open, and import an inspectable project bundle}
\description{Native R facade for a versioned local project registry. Registration records declared provenance; it never runs analysis.}
\usage{ProjectBundle}
\format{A list with \code{create(name, project_dir, purpose = NULL, raw_dir = NULL, metadata = NULL)}, \code{open(project_dir)}, and \code{import_zip(path, project_dir)}. Each returns a bundle object with snake_case methods.}
\details{\code{create} requires an existing project directory and refuses an existing registry. \code{open} reads without mutation. The returned object provides \code{read_figure_source}, \code{check_context}, \code{resolve_figure}, \code{save_figure}, \code{set_data_scope}, \code{resolve_data}, \code{register_data}, \code{register_analysis}, \code{register_figure}, \code{get_data}, \code{get_analysis}, \code{get_figure}, \code{find_figures}, \code{set_design}, \code{get_design}, \code{get_condition}, \code{get_levels}, \code{get_selected_levels}, \code{get_reference_level}, \code{get_replicate}, \code{check_design_metadata}, \code{get_design_summary}, \code{summary_text}, \code{set_current}, \code{set_context}, \code{update_record}, \code{record_decision}, \code{rebind_external}, \code{save}, \code{check}, \code{summary}, \code{status}, \code{preview_export}, and \code{export_zip}. \code{set_design} records a versioned declared study design; optional in-memory metadata checks condition and replicate columns without reading a file. \code{get_design} returns the current or exact historical revision. \code{summary_text} and printing give bounded human-readable context. \code{status(compact = TRUE)} returns a read-only, JSON-serializable status bounded to 4096 UTF-8 bytes. By default it returns metadata only. \code{check_files = TRUE} explicitly inspects at most 100 distinct relevant file/code locators; \code{missing$unchecked} counts the rest. Ordinary getters report unknown availability until explicitly checked. \code{get_figure} accepts exact references or an unambiguous asset_id/path selector and optional revision; bare IDs with multiple revisions reject. \code{compact = TRUE} returns a bounded figure-source report. Optional \code{figure_sources} declarations keep rendering inputs separate from the exact analysis. \code{read_figure_source} returns at most 1 MiB of verified preserved bytes; recorded snapshots never fall back to changed originals. Dependency completeness and execution remain unknown. \code{resolve_data(ref = NULL, purpose = NULL, verify, expected_scope = NULL, require_membership = FALSE)} requires exactly one selector and \code{verify = "sha256"}; it streams the selected file and rejects missing baselines or mismatches. \code{set_data_scope(ref, scope, reason, design_ref = NULL)} creates a DATA revision without moving current. \code{register_analysis} and standalone figures accept exact \code{design_ref} and \code{input_mode = "separate"} or explicit \code{"combined"}. Omitted design pins the project default once; explicit NULL records unknown context. \code{check_context(ref)} checks declarations only. \code{resolve_figure(ref, verify = "sha256")} checks recorded bytes before returning a path. \code{save_figure(source, type = NULL, ref = NULL, ...)} copies one existing saved figure into an exclusive managed revision; it does not execute plotting code or copy data. With ref, exact context is retained and analytical overrides reject. New analysis/figure registration stages schema 0.4.0 and requires clients >=0.5.0. Scope/design data require schema 0.3.0; earlier schemas remain readable. Clean save has no disk writes; meaningful saves preserve stale-write and atomic-publication checks. It does not hash payloads or probe URIs. \code{status(compact = FALSE)} is unsupported. Analysis and figure detail views expose \code{evidence} and missing execution evidence. Registration records declarations; hashes, snapshots and imports never establish observed execution. Compact status and summaries report this boundary without scanning records or reading payloads. Save and import writes are supported on tested local macOS filesystems.}
